cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you refer to Mandara Shell in your work, please cite it like this."
title: "Mandara Shell"
abstract: >-
  Mandara Shell is a responsive native Linux Wayland desktop shell written
  in Rust on GPUI, with spring motion, live settings and optional offline
  AI control in natural language. Ask the launcher to switch to dark mode
  or change your volume, review the action, then press Enter. CPU inference
  runs off the UI thread in a temporary worker that exits when finished or
  closed. Historical release samples built frames in about 0.1 ms; current
  memory use and AI response time depend on the workload and hardware.
  Native drivers support MangoWM, Niri, Hyprland, Umbriel, Sway, River
  Classic, KWin and Aqueous. Sandboxed WebAssembly plugins and documented commands
  with JSON replies extend the desktop.
url: "https://thehamdiz.github.io/mandara/"
type: software
